### Health Care Act 2008 (SA) Reporting Requirements

#### **1. Incident Reporting**
Health services must report incidents that result in harm or have the potential to result in harm to patients. This includes:
- **Sentinel Events**: Serious incidents that result in death or major permanent loss of function.
- **Adverse Events**: Incidents that result in harm to a patient [1](https://www.legislation.sa.gov.au/__legislation/lz/c/a/health%20care%20act%202008/current/2008.3.auth.pdf).

#### **2. Performance Reporting**
Health services must report on various health outcomes as part of their performance obligations under the Health Care Act 2008. This includes reporting on key performance indicators (KPIs) related to patient care and health outcomes [2](https://www.legislation.sa.gov.au/lz?path=%2FC%2FA%2FHEALTH%20CARE%20ACT%202008).

#### **3. Licensing and Accreditation**
Health services must comply with licensing and accreditation requirements, ensuring that facilities meet the standards set by the Health Care Act 2008 [1](https://www.legislation.sa.gov.au/__legislation/lz/c/a/health%20care%20act%202008/current/2008.3.auth.pdf).

#### **4. Annual and Four-Yearly Reports**
The Health Performance Council must submit an annual report and a four-yearly report on the performance of the health system, including recommendations for improvement [1](https://www.legislation.sa.gov.au/__legislation/lz/c/a/health%20care%20act%202008/current/2008.3.auth.pdf).

These requirements ensure comprehensive documentation, transparency, and accountability within the healthcare system, aiming to improve patient safety and care quality.

